# Component Architecture

## Directory Structure

Organize components under `src/components/` using category-based subdirectories:

```
src/components/
  ui/          # Atomic primitives: Button, Badge, Card, Icon wrappers
  layout/      # Structural shells: Header, Footer, Section, Container
  sections/    # Page-level content blocks: Hero, AboutSection, ProjectGrid, ContactForm
```

## File Conventions

- One component per file. Name the file after the component in PascalCase (e.g., `Header.tsx`).
- For components that grow beyond a single file, promote to a folder:
  ```
  Header/
    index.tsx       # Main component (re-exports)
    HeaderNav.tsx   # Sub-component
    types.ts        # Shared types/interfaces
  ```
- Colocate component-specific types in a `types.ts` file when they are shared across sub-components.
- Test files live next to the component: `Header.test.tsx`.

## Component Patterns

### Server vs Client Components

- **Default to Server Components.** They render on the server with zero client JS.
- Add `"use client"` only when the component requires:
  - Event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`, etc.)
  - React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`, etc.)
  - Browser-only APIs (`window`, `document`, `IntersectionObserver`, etc.)
- Keep client boundaries as small as possible — extract interactive parts into leaf client components.

### Props & Types

- Use `interface` for component prop definitions (better for extending and declaration merging).
- Name the interface `{ComponentName}Props`.
- Destructure props in the function signature.

```tsx
interface ButtonProps {
  variant?: "primary" | "outline";
  children: React.ReactNode;
}

export function Button({ variant = "primary", children }: ButtonProps) {
  // ...
}
```

### Composition

- Prefer composition over prop drilling. Use `children` and slot patterns.
- For section components, accept a `className` prop and merge it with internal classes using template literals or `clsx`.

## Naming Conventions

- Components: `PascalCase`
- Hooks: `camelCase` prefixed with `use` (e.g., `useMobileMenu`)
- Utility functions: `camelCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- CSS custom properties: `--kebab-case`
